# SSIMULACRA 2.1 C++ style.
#
# Google C++ layout with project overrides: four-space indentation, 81 columns,
# braces attached to the declaration line, and -- when a parameter or argument
# list does not fit on one line -- the list is broken after the open bracket,
# packed up to the column limit, and closed by a bracket on its own line:
#
#     void axis_taps(
#         uint out_pos, float scale, float shift, uint dim,
#         out float weights[SS2_TAPS], out int indices[SS2_TAPS], out float total
#     ) {
#
# The three dangling-bracket keys are recent: verified on clang-format 23.1.3.
# An older release warns about them as unknown keys and then falls back to
# Google's attached bracket, so pin the version before trusting a --dry-run.
#
# Pointer/reference alignment is stated explicitly so it does not drift with the
# clang-format version. Includes are left exactly as written: the GLSL sources
# are formatted by this same config (clang-format has no GLSL grammar, it lexes
# them as C++), and sorting there would move common.glsl after the files that
# include it.
#
# Usage: rg --files -0 -g '*.cc' -g '*.h' -g '*.cu' -g '*.comp' -g '*.glsl' \
#          src include cli tests bench tools/image_io | xargs -0 clang-format -i
---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: Google
Standard: c++20
ColumnLimit: 81
IndentWidth: 4
ContinuationIndentWidth: 4
AccessModifierOffset: -4
BreakBeforeBraces: Attach
BinPackParameters: BinPack
BinPackArguments: BinPack
BreakAfterOpenBracketFunction: true
BreakBeforeCloseBracketFunction: true
SortIncludes: Never
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Left
